WEBVTT

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:34.614
So, there it is, people.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.066
Due to budget cutbacks,

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:39.403
we will no longer be offering
free squid guts in the kitchen.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:44.741
Oh, boo-hoo.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.332
Everyone, look at
my latest invention!

00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:48.457
Okay.

00:00:48.549 --> 00:00:50.881
I like how it's not
killing us so far.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:54.460
It takes any object
and makes two smaller copies.

00:00:54.805 --> 00:00:56.511
All right!

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.095
Why?

00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:59.889
You see, as I age,

00:00:59.977 --> 00:01:02.719
I've been shrinking
and feeling colder.

00:01:02.813 --> 00:01:07.056
So now I need twice as many
sweaters, in a smaller size.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.983
First, I scan
the old sweater.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.811
Then we add some matter.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.363
Any old,
useless matter will do.

00:01:18.954 --> 00:01:21.991
Now the matter prism
reorganizes the raw material

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.073
into two smaller copies.

00:01:27.004 --> 00:01:29.370
So, that's where
baby sweaters come from.

00:01:32.676 --> 00:01:35.008
Enclosed as a PDF attachment,

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:38.258
a picture of yourself,
in a boat, on a river.

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:41.090
It's a river that
flows in two directions.

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:42.344
Make that three.

00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:44.392
It's a magic river,
that's how.

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:47.221
And it's flowing down
the eerie canal to

00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:49.268
The Scary Door.

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:51.896
That's "eerie" with two E's.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.270
Consider,
if you have the energy,

00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:58.949
Dr. Daniel Zenus, an inventor
with a terminal case

00:01:59.036 --> 00:02:00.321
of"The Lazies."

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:02.781
This robot will do
everything for me.

00:02:02.873 --> 00:02:05.831
Robot, activate yourself
and do my research.

00:02:11.048 --> 00:02:12.037
Ahh.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.917
Next, assume
my social obligations.

00:02:23.644 --> 00:02:24.679
Dr. Zenus,

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:27.136
for a lifetime of
scientific achievement,

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:30.643
we present this award
to your robot.

00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:33.608
Daddy, I love you.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.231
Lf only
I'd programmed the robot

00:02:39.326 --> 00:02:41.442
to be more careful
what I wished for.

00:02:41.536 --> 00:02:44.619
Robot, experience
this tragic irony for me.

00:02:45.082 --> 00:02:47.664
No!

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:51.826
Ahh.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.079
Ahh.

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:57.040
Man, I wish we had
a robot to do stuff.

00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:58.124
I know, right?

00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:01.719
Bender, thank God
I found you in time.

00:03:02.032 --> 00:03:06.116
I need someone in the lab
immediately to fold my new sweaters.

00:03:06.328 --> 00:03:09.991
I'm sorry, do you see a robot
in this room named "Folder"?

00:03:11.666 --> 00:03:15.705
Fortunately, I came prepared
with a back-up phrasing.

00:03:16.004 --> 00:03:19.417
Bender, would you mind
bending my new sweaters?

00:03:19.508 --> 00:03:20.668
There's only
two of them.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:21.961
Wait.

00:03:22.052 --> 00:03:23.792
You want me to
do two things?

00:03:23.887 --> 00:03:27.425
Man, I'd call my lawyer if dialing
a phone wasn't such a hassle.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.932
Razza frazza two things.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:34.178
Ooh, razza frazza duplicator.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.481
Now for some tasty matter.

00:03:49.412 --> 00:03:51.528
Howdy, fellas.
I'm Bender.

00:03:51.623 --> 00:03:53.238
Go to hell, old man!

00:03:53.416 --> 00:03:55.372
I like your attitude.
Let's party.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.291
But first,
fold these two sweaters.

00:03:58.129 --> 00:04:00.245
I'm sorry,
do you see a robot

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.501
in this room
named "Folder"?

00:04:03.927 --> 00:04:05.087
Damn, you're cute.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.543
Hi. I'm Bender.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.713
This is my robot Bender, and
this is my other robot Bender.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:44.835
Oh, Lord.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:47.880
They're 60% scale
replicas of me, Bender.

00:04:47.971 --> 00:04:50.883
Does that mean they only
do 60% of the work you do,

00:04:50.974 --> 00:04:52.805
or that they actually
do more work

00:04:52.976 --> 00:04:54.807
because they're only
60% as lazy?

00:04:57.147 --> 00:04:58.387
Shut up.

00:04:58.481 --> 00:05:00.221
That's a good one.

00:05:00.317 --> 00:05:02.023
Enough good ones, everyone.

00:05:02.319 --> 00:05:05.106
We have a delivery to
an alien space giant.

00:05:05.196 --> 00:05:06.606
You'll have to
be respectful.

00:05:06.698 --> 00:05:10.156
This customer is 50-feet tall and
sensitive about his appearance.

00:05:10.744 --> 00:05:13.827
Colossal tooth whitener,
mega deodorant,

00:05:13.914 --> 00:05:16.576
humungous acne cream, aww,

00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:18.539
and one
regular-sized condom.

00:05:18.627 --> 00:05:22.461
All that and a small wiener?
This guy's got it goin' on!

00:05:35.894 --> 00:05:38.852
Remember, don't show any
reaction to his appearance.

00:05:43.693 --> 00:05:46.981
I hope that's vanishing cream,
'cause that needs to go away.

00:05:48.239 --> 00:05:49.354
That's cold-blooded!

00:05:49.379 --> 00:05:50.368
Shh!

00:05:50.533 --> 00:05:52.615
Lt's okay.
I understand.

00:05:52.702 --> 00:05:54.784
My unusual appearance
makes people nervous.

00:05:54.871 --> 00:05:56.702
You used humor
to defuse the tension.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.873
Yep, and there's still a little
more tension. So, look out!

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.991
You so ugly,

00:06:02.087 --> 00:06:05.045
when trick-or-treaters come to
your house, they give you candy.

00:06:05.173 --> 00:06:07.334
You so ugly,
when you go to the bank,

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:09.628
they ask you to
put on a ski mask!

00:06:09.761 --> 00:06:12.878
You so ugly, you
cracked The Daily Mirror.

00:06:12.973 --> 00:06:14.509
It's a newspaper!

00:06:16.226 --> 00:06:19.593
I wish it weren't so, but
many of these things are true.

00:06:19.688 --> 00:06:21.895
Anyhow, you've lowered
my self-esteem a bit more,

00:06:21.982 --> 00:06:24.189
but I'm sincerely grateful
you came all this way

00:06:24.275 --> 00:06:25.856
to deliver my fungus chisel.

00:06:25.944 --> 00:06:28.401
Don't feel bad, sir.
It's not your fault.

00:06:28.571 --> 00:06:30.687
You probably just
inherited your appearance

00:06:30.782 --> 00:06:32.363
from your mother.
What?

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.611
No one
insults my mama!

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.758
God, shield your eyes!

00:06:52.846 --> 00:06:55.258
Lt's like Edward
James Olmos on IMAX!

00:07:01.855 --> 00:07:04.517
Did you see his face
when I said he so ugly?

00:07:04.607 --> 00:07:07.223
No, I blacked out,
'cause he so ugly!

00:07:09.029 --> 00:07:12.567
Hey, guys, quit reminiscing
and grab me two cigars.

00:07:12.657 --> 00:07:13.646
One thing each?

00:07:13.742 --> 00:07:14.731
Sounds fair.

00:07:14.826 --> 00:07:16.782
Wait, make that
four cigars.

00:07:17.287 --> 00:07:19.494
You want us
to do four things?

00:07:26.046 --> 00:07:27.582
My Manwich!

00:07:30.133 --> 00:07:31.998
What's up, shorty?

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:35.005
And that's the story
of how one of me became two,

00:07:35.096 --> 00:07:37.712
and two became four,
making seven total.

00:07:37.807 --> 00:07:39.138
The end.

00:07:41.352 --> 00:07:43.217
I just like
having the end locker.

00:07:43.313 --> 00:07:45.349
It's not like Amy
cares about it at all.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.476
But no, she won't trade with me.

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:48.556
A rat!

00:07:48.651 --> 00:07:49.891
Yes, she is a rat.

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:51.976
No, look!

00:07:52.197 --> 00:07:53.812
Which way
to the tiny hookers?

00:07:55.825 --> 00:07:57.611
A big, fat roach!

00:07:57.702 --> 00:07:59.408
What?
I thought I put that away.

00:07:59.496 --> 00:08:01.407
No, there!

00:08:02.832 --> 00:08:03.867
Who are you?

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.080
Bender sent me.

00:08:11.841 --> 00:08:13.627
Hey, I know that guy.

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:24.392
Scruffy, what is that tiny
Bender doing in my soup?

00:08:24.687 --> 00:08:27.645
Lt appears to be giving you
the finger, sir. Enjoy.

00:08:27.816 --> 00:08:31.354
Help me, help me!
I'm too lazy to escape!

00:08:37.492 --> 00:08:38.481
Ow!

00:08:47.277 --> 00:08:47.901
What?

00:08:48.018 --> 00:08:49.609
This place
is crawling with yous!

00:08:50.113 --> 00:08:51.853
So there's more
Benders around.

00:08:51.948 --> 00:08:54.314
As far as I'm concerned,
that's good news.

00:08:54.409 --> 00:08:55.694
Bad news, everyone.

00:08:55.869 --> 00:08:57.575
Look at this
infinite series

00:08:57.662 --> 00:09:01.200
representing the mass of
successive generations of Benders.

00:09:06.838 --> 00:09:07.873
Don't wait for me.

00:09:07.964 --> 00:09:09.955
It's non-convergent!

00:09:10.133 --> 00:09:11.373
Oh, dip!

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:13.507
Unless we quickly
exterminate them,

00:09:13.595 --> 00:09:15.677
they'll replicate
ad Infinitum

00:09:15.764 --> 00:09:18.471
and consume
all the matter on Earth.

00:09:20.351 --> 00:09:24.435
According to my calculations, there
are 11 generations at the moment.

00:09:24.522 --> 00:09:28.185
That's 2,046 total Benders
we need to destroy.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:30.350
Wait, does that include me?

00:09:36.868 --> 00:09:39.325
Too bad he didn't
have his own Bible.

00:09:39.496 --> 00:09:42.579
Just 2,045 more to go.

00:09:49.089 --> 00:09:51.080
Creatures have taken
over my house

00:09:51.174 --> 00:09:53.460
They want my food
and my skin and my time

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.172
Little frogs are okay
but the slugs on the rug

00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:58.753
Send me out of my mind

00:09:59.182 --> 00:10:01.468
There's no place else
that I can go

00:10:01.726 --> 00:10:03.512
The only thing
I can turn to is

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:05.184
Rock 'n'Roll Pest Control

00:10:05.271 --> 00:10:06.761
A- wha-ho
A- wha-ho Wha-ho

00:10:06.856 --> 00:10:10.269
Rock 'n'Roll Pest Control

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:11.850
A- wha-ho
A- wha-ho Wha-ho

00:10:11.945 --> 00:10:13.276
Rock 'n'Roll Pest Control

00:10:13.363 --> 00:10:14.569
All right!

00:10:19.202 --> 00:10:22.285
Two thousand
forty five, 2,046.

00:10:22.372 --> 00:10:24.658
That's it. We got 'em all
except for the big one.

00:10:24.749 --> 00:10:27.081
Wait, this isn't
a real Bender.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:30.077
It's a talking doll from
when Bender had that sitcom

00:10:30.171 --> 00:10:32.537
about the city robot
who moves back to the farm.

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:35.210
Shut your pumpkin, bumpkin.

00:10:37.303 --> 00:10:40.386
All right, so I let
one measly Bender get away.

00:10:40.473 --> 00:10:43.806
How much harm can one infinitely
self-reproducing robot do?

00:10:43.977 --> 00:10:46.593
Bender! How could you be
so lazy and irresponsible?

00:10:47.772 --> 00:10:50.058
Hey. What? Did someone say I'm great?

00:10:54.112 --> 00:10:56.023
What's with the gray goo?

00:10:57.173 --> 00:10:59.038
Bite my tiny metal ass!

00:10:59.467 --> 00:11:02.049
Hey, those jerklings
ate my couch.

00:11:02.387 --> 00:11:05.720
God! We've opened
Pandora's fly.

00:11:05.807 --> 00:11:07.343
They'll reproduce
without limit,

00:11:07.433 --> 00:11:10.015
consuming all
the matter in the world!

00:11:10.186 --> 00:11:12.017
Like the Kardashians.

00:11:15.483 --> 00:11:18.975
Now they drank my booze?
They've gone too far!

00:11:19.195 --> 00:11:22.437
Wait a second. All Benders
are powered by alcohol!

00:11:22.532 --> 00:11:23.567
Of course.

00:11:23.866 --> 00:11:26.278
Long before
the Benders devour the Earth,

00:11:26.369 --> 00:11:29.202
they'll deplete the
planet's booze and die off.

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.742
This is a problem
that will solve itself.

00:11:31.916 --> 00:11:33.702
A problem
that solves itself?

00:11:33.793 --> 00:11:36.409
That sounds like
a job for me, Bender.

00:11:39.882 --> 00:11:41.167
Our top story,

00:11:41.259 --> 00:11:44.797
all alcohol on Earth
has mysteriously disappeared.

00:11:44.887 --> 00:11:46.627
Consequences are minimal,

00:11:46.723 --> 00:11:49.089
except among
the most hardened alcoholics.

00:11:49.684 --> 00:11:50.221
Linda?

00:11:50.246 --> 00:11:53.760
I can no longer
face my children!

00:11:55.648 --> 00:11:56.808
Crisis averted.

00:11:56.899 --> 00:11:59.436
Without alcohol, the
Benders are dying off.

00:12:04.657 --> 00:12:07.148
A greater tragedy
my eyes have never beheld.

00:12:07.368 --> 00:12:09.404
Well, into the toilet.

00:12:13.416 --> 00:12:16.624
So sober, so weak.

00:12:16.836 --> 00:12:19.498
Things really worked
out nicely this time.

00:12:25.261 --> 00:12:27.877
This doesn't taste
like old-man water.

00:12:28.222 --> 00:12:30.713
Everyone to
the situation room!

00:12:31.601 --> 00:12:33.762
I was lying here snoozing,

00:12:33.853 --> 00:12:37.345
dreaming, oddly enough,
about bathing in champagne

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.182
with six of the world's
most distinguished scientists,

00:12:40.276 --> 00:12:41.516
when suddenly,

00:12:41.611 --> 00:12:45.445
I realized my bathwater had
been transformed into alcohol.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.946
Alcohol?

00:12:52.246 --> 00:12:54.111
Chug, chug,
chug, chug!

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.451
Chug, chug, chug,
chug, chug!

00:12:56.584 --> 00:12:57.573
Mmm!

00:12:57.668 --> 00:13:01.707
Lt's like fine cognac
with a hint of aged scrotum.

00:13:02.507 --> 00:13:03.792
How can this be?

00:13:03.883 --> 00:13:06.795
I thought the Benders drank
all the alcohol in the world.

00:13:06.886 --> 00:13:09.343
They did,
but then they made more!

00:13:10.807 --> 00:13:14.470
You see, once the Benders
reached atomic scale,

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:18.724
they began directly manipulating
water and CO2 molecules

00:13:18.815 --> 00:13:20.396
to make alcohol.

00:13:23.403 --> 00:13:24.609
In a matter of hours,

00:13:24.695 --> 00:13:27.562
there will be no more
fresh water on Earth.

00:13:29.325 --> 00:13:32.738
No! What will I
mix with my scotch?

00:13:39.168 --> 00:13:40.954
Hey, you!

00:13:41.838 --> 00:13:43.328
Good evening.

00:13:43.423 --> 00:13:46.381
Who are you calling drunk?
You're not drunk. I'm drunk.

00:13:46.843 --> 00:13:48.174
That's right, Linda.

00:13:48.261 --> 00:13:50.718
Water is now booze,

00:13:50.805 --> 00:13:53.842
and everyone's tiddy much
protally fit-shaced.

00:13:55.351 --> 00:13:59.435
Turning to sports,
the Indy 500 was today.

00:13:59.522 --> 00:14:01.513
There were no survivors.

00:14:03.693 --> 00:14:06.560
This chair is so comfortable.

00:14:08.114 --> 00:14:10.196
Classic Amy.

00:14:11.075 --> 00:14:12.815
You want to see
a picture of my boy?

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:13.945
Sure.

00:14:15.204 --> 00:14:16.444
That's your penis.

00:14:16.581 --> 00:14:17.821
That's my boy.

00:14:18.166 --> 00:14:20.999
I guess this isn't
not so bad.

00:14:21.252 --> 00:14:24.039
As long as we don't need
to use our mental...

00:14:24.172 --> 00:14:25.252
Mental...

00:14:25.381 --> 00:14:26.370
Minds?

00:14:26.507 --> 00:14:27.542
What?

00:14:37.643 --> 00:14:39.099
No, listen.

00:14:39.187 --> 00:14:41.303
I freaking love you.

00:14:41.439 --> 00:14:43.395
And I don't throw
that word around.

00:14:43.524 --> 00:14:44.980
I know you don't.

00:14:45.067 --> 00:14:47.854
That's why I love you.

00:14:47.945 --> 00:14:50.402
Are the pizza muffins
ready?

00:14:52.533 --> 00:14:54.615
He's here for revenging,
that's why!

00:14:54.702 --> 00:14:57.409
No!
Wait! I'm here to apologize.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.912
For your looks?

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.660
Nice one.

00:15:01.751 --> 00:15:04.493
Well, yes, actually, it
is sort of related to that.

00:15:04.587 --> 00:15:05.747
Can we talk?

00:15:05.922 --> 00:15:08.334
Grabbing your spaceship was not okay.

00:15:08.549 --> 00:15:11.962
I lost my cool,
and I'm sorry.

00:15:12.094 --> 00:15:14.551
In group, I learned
that I tend to be a bit...

00:15:14.764 --> 00:15:16.095
Repulsive?

00:15:16.182 --> 00:15:17.388
Sensitive.

00:15:17.475 --> 00:15:20.091
So now I'm, like, trying
to work on my attitude,

00:15:20.186 --> 00:15:22.393
and project
an air of positivity.

00:15:22.522 --> 00:15:24.683
You're projecting
an alr of something.

00:15:24.774 --> 00:15:25.809
Phew!

00:15:26.275 --> 00:15:30.063
You're so stinky, you need
Right Guard and left guard.

00:15:30.363 --> 00:15:32.445
I'll take your
hygiene advice to heart.

00:15:32.573 --> 00:15:34.780
You're ugly!

00:15:35.785 --> 00:15:37.776
Hey! Ow!

00:15:38.412 --> 00:15:39.948
Yo, freak show!

00:15:40.122 --> 00:15:43.614
Your face has been declared
a weapon of mass disgusting.

00:15:43.751 --> 00:15:45.742
Timeless.

00:15:45.962 --> 00:15:48.294
Okay, deep breath,
deep breath.

00:15:53.636 --> 00:15:55.001
Dr. Lesterman?

00:15:55.096 --> 00:15:56.051
I'm sorry to bother you,

00:15:56.138 --> 00:15:58.971
but I think I'm close
to a temper-control incident.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.385
You have reached the office

00:16:00.476 --> 00:16:03.343
of Dr. Judy Lesterman
and Dr. Ira Rothkiss.

00:16:03.437 --> 00:16:05.098
The office
is now closed.

00:16:05.314 --> 00:16:07.020
If this is
a pharmacy calling...

00:16:10.152 --> 00:16:14.065
That's it! I promised myself
I wouldn't do this, but...

00:16:16.659 --> 00:16:18.195
I will destroy you all!

00:16:18.369 --> 00:16:23.659
I won't stop until your whole planet
is as ugly as you perceive me to be!

00:16:23.833 --> 00:16:26.119
That will take
a very long time.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.668
Okay. Stop! Stop!

00:16:33.884 --> 00:16:34.964
Stupid...

00:16:39.348 --> 00:16:42.260
Blender, you're the
only one who's sober.

00:16:42.351 --> 00:16:43.807
You got to do something!

00:16:43.894 --> 00:16:45.850
Haven't I done
enough already?

00:16:46.188 --> 00:16:49.806
Please, stop the monster.
Just do that one thing!

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.891
Make it zero,
and you got a deal.

00:16:52.153 --> 00:16:55.862
What if I foldeded the
Professor's sweaters for you?

00:16:55.948 --> 00:16:57.063
Both of them?

00:16:57.199 --> 00:17:00.612
You mean you'll do two things,
and I only have to do one thing?

00:17:00.703 --> 00:17:02.739
Yeah. Just save the world.

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:05.575
Sucker.

00:17:08.044 --> 00:17:10.660
Legion of Benders,
come unto me!

00:17:10.755 --> 00:17:12.916
We have one thing to do.

00:17:13.215 --> 00:17:14.500
Screw that!

00:17:14.592 --> 00:17:16.128
Come on,
you lazy jerks!

00:17:16.218 --> 00:17:17.458
Lf we all pitch in,

00:17:17.553 --> 00:17:20.386
we each only have to do
one quintilllonth of a thing.

00:17:20.848 --> 00:17:22.679
All right.

00:17:39.617 --> 00:17:41.027
Whoa.

00:17:45.915 --> 00:17:49.078
Big Bender starts right now.

00:17:53.589 --> 00:17:55.295
Get a shave, ugly!

00:17:56.092 --> 00:17:57.081
Oh.

00:18:02.598 --> 00:18:04.589
How about some aftershave, dumpy?

00:18:05.309 --> 00:18:06.424
You big bully!

00:18:06.644 --> 00:18:09.807
You ugly nerd, enjoy a
nice Guggenheim swirly!

00:18:18.531 --> 00:18:20.522
Let this beating be a lesson

00:18:20.616 --> 00:18:23.779
about never attacking those
more handsome than oneself.

00:18:24.745 --> 00:18:27.657
All I wanted was
to apologize to you people.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.872
But now
I have to kill you.

00:18:30.084 --> 00:18:32.700
How, by making me look at you?

00:18:32.795 --> 00:18:35.582
No. By making you
look at my mama!

00:18:35.673 --> 00:18:36.708
Ah!

00:18:36.799 --> 00:18:38.414
Your mama's so ugly!

00:18:38.509 --> 00:18:41.091
I told you not to
talk about my mama!

00:19:01.198 --> 00:19:03.439
Walk toward the light, Bender.

00:19:03.534 --> 00:19:05.991
Man, do I have to walk?

00:19:06.245 --> 00:19:07.781
No!

00:19:13.169 --> 00:19:14.158
Huh?

00:19:18.466 --> 00:19:20.331
No!

00:19:22.845 --> 00:19:25.086
At last I'm beautiful!

00:19:26.432 --> 00:19:29.094
Yeah,
if you're into gray dust.

00:19:32.438 --> 00:19:34.144
Bender, you di' it!

00:19:34.231 --> 00:19:36.267
No, we di' it.

00:19:37.067 --> 00:19:38.307
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:19:38.402 --> 00:19:42.020
if, together we were able to
defeat this giant space monster,

00:19:42.239 --> 00:19:44.025
think how also
we might defeat

00:19:44.116 --> 00:19:47.734
the monsters of poverty
and disease and unliteracy.

00:19:48.204 --> 00:19:51.116
In this spirit,
I ask my fellow Benders

00:19:51.207 --> 00:19:53.323
to join me in
working diligently to...

00:19:53.417 --> 00:19:54.782
Boo!

00:19:54.919 --> 00:19:56.284
Go to hell!

00:19:56.378 --> 00:19:57.959
Come on, let's go someplace

00:19:58.047 --> 00:20:01.380
where we don't have to do one
quintillionth of a thing all the time.

00:20:15.105 --> 00:20:16.720
Well, that was dumb.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:24.816
Man, were we drunk.

00:20:24.907 --> 00:20:26.363
What happened, Professor?

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:29.408
Something
absolutely incredible!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.656
The sweaters got folded!

00:20:33.082 --> 00:20:34.162
But how?

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:35.490
I didn't do it.

00:20:35.584 --> 00:20:38.417
Bender, did you learn a
lesson about not being lazy

00:20:38.546 --> 00:20:40.912
while the rest of us were
bombed out of our gourds?

00:20:41.006 --> 00:20:42.587
Maybe I did, Fry.

00:20:42.675 --> 00:20:44.506
Maybe I did.

00:20:44.593 --> 00:20:46.925
Or maybe I rescued
one last mini-Bender

00:20:47.012 --> 00:20:50.846
to fold stupid, ugly sweaters
while I laughed at him.

00:20:51.308 --> 00:20:53.299
I guess we'll never know.